From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:04:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: keep power save buffering for nullfunc probes

Nullfunc frames from the pending path go to the PSD queue, which
transmits at once, without power save buffering. A nullfunc frame that
probes a station (NL80211_CMD_PROBE_CLIENT, which hostapd uses to check
an inactive station) is then sent while the station sleeps: it is not
acknowledged, and hostapd disconnects the station.

Send a nullfunc frame to the PSD queue only when mac80211 marked it as
not to be buffered (IEEE80211_TX_CTL_NO_PS_BUFFER), as it does for the
response to a station in power save.

Fixes: da6d90e4f66a ("wifi: mt76: route nullfunc frames to PSD/ALTX queue")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
--- a/tx.c
+++ b/tx.c
@@ -680,6 +680,22 @@ void mt76_txq_schedule(struct mt76_phy *
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mt76_txq_schedule);
 
+static bool
+mt76_tx_skip_ps_buffer(struct sk_buff *skb)
+{
+	struct ieee80211_hdr *hdr = (struct ieee80211_hdr *)skb->data;
+
+	/*
+	 * A nullfunc frame that answers a station in power save must go out
+	 * at once; one that probes a station waits until the station is
+	 * awake, as any other data frame.
+	 */
+	if (ieee80211_is_data(hdr->frame_control))
+		return IEEE80211_SKB_CB(skb)->flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_NO_PS_BUFFER;
+
+	return !ieee80211_is_bufferable_mmpdu(skb);
+}
+
 static int
 mt76_txq_schedule_pending_wcid(struct mt76_phy *phy, struct mt76_wcid *wcid,
 			       struct sk_buff_head *head)
@@ -700,7 +716,7 @@ mt76_txq_schedule_pending_wcid(struct mt
 		    !(info->flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_HW_80211_ENCAP) &&
 		    !ieee80211_is_data_present(hdr->frame_control) &&
 		    (!(wcid->tx_info & MT_WCID_TX_INFO_SET) ||
-		     !ieee80211_is_bufferable_mmpdu(skb) ||
+		     mt76_tx_skip_ps_buffer(skb) ||
 		     ieee80211_is_deauth(hdr->frame_control) ||
 		     ieee80211_is_disassoc(hdr->frame_control) ||
 		     head == &wcid->tx_offchannel))
